<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rawanduz</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rawandiz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rawanduz is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erbil">Erbil</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> in Iraqi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurdistan">Kurdistan</a>, set on a rock above the deep gorge of the Rawanduz river near the Gali Ali Beg canyon. It was the capital of the Kurdish Soran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>, which under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mir-muhammad-kor">Mir Muhammad Kor</a> in the early 19th century made it a centre of arms production and military power, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> ended the emirate in 1836.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rawanduz.jpg" alt="Rawanduz" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Claus Weinberg · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rawanduz_-_Kurdistan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
